=== CP-7 test harness setup and fake transport ===
     1	"""CP-7 integration — the WHOLE PAPER loop on a fixture clock against the fake
     2	Toobit responder (a test double only; nothing here reaches a network).
     3
     4	Composition root, one event loop, one ledger writer (Ch.23 L18253–18260):
     5
     6	    FixtureClock (UTC, deterministic, monotone)
     7	      → StartupReconciliation: STARTING → SELF_TEST → RECONCILING → READY
     8	        (nine SBOM pins, schema version, clock drift, ladder state, then the
     9	        broker reconciliation against the fake venue)
    10	      → Scheduler: the 140-cell grid, semaphore 4, the nine contract stages,
    11	        HTF last-closed only, leverage = min over ALL caps
    12	      → the ``execution`` stage hands the CP-6 proposal + adjudication to
    13	        build_trade_plan → ExecutionFSM.submit → ToobitAdapter (5 operations,
    14	        signed) → the fake responder → ACK/fill
    15	      → record_fill → place_protection (STOP + LIMIT, GTC, reduceOnly) →
    16	        activate_management → close_position (stop-gap attribution, OUTCOME) →
    17	        reconcile (T_MATCH / T-LR-002 / T-LR-003) → RECONCILED
    18	      → the ledger single writer appends every event; verify_chain() recomputes
    19	        every payload hash and the parent linkage at the end
    20	      → EventBus → the alert bridge → SignalingPlane (token bucket, idempotency,
    21	        retry, durable outbox, Agg-only in-memory chart) → the fake transport
    22	      → ControlPlane: OWNER/USER roles, Busy Guard, Emergency ratchet + nonce,
    23	        Panic Lock, update_id replay — every effect through the handler seam.
    24
    25	Also asserted: a drifted clock boots DEGRADED and NO cell runs; a lost ack ends
    26	in RECOVERY_REQUIRED with a P0 alert and exactly one submission (never a
    27	resubmit); the loop is deterministic over two independent runs; no secret
    28	material reaches the ledger, the wire or a Telegram message.
    29	"""
