=== Normative execution/F3 PAPER simulator clauses ===
 16866	## 16. Execution, Venue Adapter, and Ledger
 16867
 16868	**Session-CP-14 (2026-09-18; D34 / ISSUE-044):** ADV is mean daily base-asset volume from CLOSED 1h bars over the previous 30 complete UTC days, costs use actual round-trip fees and side-specific nonnegative funding across publicly verified settlement intervals within the governed holding horizon, endpoint/schedule failure yields FUNDING_UNAVAILABLE for retry, and unavailable spread retains cost_R >= 0.05.
 16869
 16870	The execution state machine is the only path to Toobit. Identity is `intent_id` (UUIDv7) as `clientOrderId`. Unknown venue outcomes are reconciled, never blindly retried. The ledger is append-only.
 16871
 16872	### 16.1 State machine and adapter
 16873
 16874	- The execution FSM is exactly the frozen state list of the System Overview:
 16875	  `READY → SUBMITTING → ACKNOWLEDGED → PARTIAL → FILLED → PROTECTED →
 16876	  MANAGED → CLOSED → RECONCILED`, with `RECOVERY_REQUIRED` on fill timeout
 16877	  (Error Codes E-EXEC-001).
 16878	- **Reconciliation is a first-class invariant, not a background task:** no
 16879	  downstream state may advance to `RECONCILED` while ledger and exchange
 16880	  state disagree; divergence forces `RECOVERY_REQUIRED`.
 16881	- **Ledger is immutable and hash-chained** (the Data Plane `ledger` table:
 16882	  `payload_hash`, `parent_ids`, `until`); silent rewriting is forbidden —
 16883	  corrections append a revision.
 16884	- Idempotency: `intent_id / order_id / fill_id / cancel_id` identity per the
 16885	  ledger DDL; every submission carries a SHA-256-based idempotency key
 16886	  (pattern per Chapter 6 System Contract: `SHA-256(signal_id + timestamp_UTC
 16887	  + chat_id)` at the Telegram layer; execution-layer key formula is a design
 16888	  deliverable and MUST follow the same SHA-256 + TTL discipline).
 16889
 16890	Acceptance tests: `T_LEDGER` (covert insert/modify of a ledger record breaks
 16891	the hash chain) and `T_RECONCILE` (forced divergence ⇒ RECOVERY_REQUIRED).
 16892
 16893	**FSM state semantics.**
 16894
 16895	| State | Authorized meaning |
 16896	|---|---|
 16897	| READY | plan received, pre-submission validation |
 16898	| SUBMITTING | order submission in progress |
 16899	| ACKNOWLEDGED | exchange acknowledgement received |
 16900	| PARTIAL | partial fill |
 16901	| FILLED | full fill |
 16902	| PROTECTED | stop/target orders placed |
 16903	| MANAGED | Playbook management active (trailing, time exit) |
 16904	| CLOSED | position closed |
 16905	| RECONCILED | ledger ↔ exchange fully matched |
 16906	| RECOVERY_REQUIRED | divergence or fill timeout (E-EXEC-001); reconcile-first recovery |
 17020	**Session-A P3 (2026-09-17; D1/D2 — normative, owns the PAPER execution
 17021	transport):** in PAPER the venue wire above is replaced by the **PAPER
 17022	simulator**: the same five-operation surface (`submit_order`,
 17023	`cancel_order`, `query_order_state`, `query_open_positions`,
 17024	`query_account_margin_health`) off the same `fsm.submit`/`seal` path and
 17025	the same ledger, FSM, and reconcile-first law — but the `Transport` seam
 17026	is a simulator with **no network packet and no signature** (fills from
 17027	last-closed prices; the fake-responder path shape is the test double, not
 17028	the venue). The W.6 Phase-2 line "PAPER orders require
 17029	`APEX_ALLOW_SIGNED=1`" permits the PAPER loop to run; it **never**
 17030	authorizes a venue packet (ISSUE-SESSION-A-004). Constructing a signed
 17031	packet in PAPER is a defect; in LIVE the signed Wave-In wire above is the
 17032	only transport.
 17033
 17034	**Session-A F3 (2026-09-17 — normative PAPER simulator fill law, CP-15
 17035	builds it; nothing here is guessed):** (a) an entry fills at the last
 17036	CLOSED store bar's close at submit time, adjusted by the frozen cost
 17037	model — fee `0.02 %` per side (`apex/research/backtest.py`
 17038	`FEE_FRACTION = 0.0002`) plus `alpha_spread` slippage
 17039	(`alpha_spread = 0.25`, same file), the same constants the frozen
 17040	backtest cost model uses; (b) protective stop and target orders are
 17041	evaluated against each subsequent CLOSED bar with the X.4 precedence
 17042	hard stop → target → time stop (`_resolve_exit`: a bar touching the stop
 17043	is a stop-out, never a target fill), filled at the stop/target price —
 17044	a gap-through fills at the bar open; (c) `query_open_positions`,
 17045	`query_order_state` (scope `open` | `fills`), and
 17046	`query_account_margin_health` answer from the simulator's own durable
 17047	state, so `reconcile_boot` reaches READY without any network; (d) balance
 17048	= `params/paper_account_v1.yaml` `capital_usdt` + realised P/L from the
 17049	ledger; **Session-CP-14 (2026-09-17), D29, binding for CP-15:** the simulator's
 17050	`query_account_margin_health` must return exactly `(C-N)/C` from its durable
 17051	state, where C is that PAPER balance and N is gross marked open PAPER
 17052	notional plus full unfilled risk-increasing order notional, excluding
 17053	reduce-only reservations and filled-quantity double counting, with no
 17054	leverage discount. Apply P7's strictly-below 0.60 warning, 0.40 action/veto
 17055	14, and 0.20 liquidation-approach/Emergency L3 CANCEL_ALL thresholds;
 17056	missing marks/order state, C <= 0 or a fraction outside [0,1] fails closed,
 17057	never clipped. This is the PAPER reservation proxy, not exchange liquidation
 17058	distance; exposure caps remain independent and LIVE is unchanged; (e) simulator state is persisted in
 17059	the same SQLite file under the additive table `paper_sim_state`
 17060	(ADR-P2-003 additive migration; CP-15 defines its columns against the
 17061	five-op surface above), so a restart reconciles against it; (f) LIVE is
 17062	unchanged — the signed Wave-In wire stays the only LIVE transport.
